44: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:
45:     """
46:     Slide every foreground object horizontally to the right until it settles against the border or another settled object.
47: 
48:     Input structure
49:     - The grid has a dominant background color and several separate 4-connected foreground objects.
50:     - Each foreground object is a small multicolor rectangle-like sprite on the same canvas.
51:     - Objects may overlap in their row ranges, so rightward movement can make a left object stop behind a right object.
52: 
53:     Rule
54:     - Treat each 4-connected foreground object as a rigid sprite.
55:     - Simultaneously move every sprite one column right whenever its next cells are inside the grid and not blocked by a sprite that cannot move.
56:     - Repeat the simultaneous move until no sprite can move; preserve each sprite's internal colors and shape.
57: 
58:     Key insight
